[36m@@ -0,0 +1,218 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# S1 Emulator Spike Implementation Plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Goal:** Measure whether libghostty-vt 0.2.2 (pinned ghostty a887df42) can serve as tmls-rs's authoritative emulator *and* snapshot source: feed recorded and adversarial terminal streams, snapshot via `fmt::Formatter` (`Format::Vt`) at arbitrary and at sequence-aligned byte boundaries, restore into a fresh terminal, continue the stream, and compare cell-for-cell with an uninterrupted run; report mismatch classes, snapshot sizes and timings; probe portability of the VT snapshot into a second emulator (pyte).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Architecture:** New crate `spikes/s1` in the workspace. `corpus` = recorded `script` sessions (vim, btop, less, cargo, git, nested tmux, a short Claude Code session) + generated adversarial streams. `grid` = a plain-Rust `Grid` struct (rows × cells: graphemes, fg, bg, style flags, wide/spacer) extracted from `render::RenderState`, plus `TermState` (cursor x/y/visible/style, active screen, modes bitmap, title, pwd, kitty flags, scrollback_rows). `splitter` = a tiny VT state machine (same shape as `spikes/s0/src/ack.rs` stripper) that marks sequence-complete byte offsets. `experiment` = for each (stream, split, strategy) run A→snapshot→C vs D and diff; `report` = Markdown + JSON. A Python helper feeds the VT snapshot to pyte and compares plain text.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Tech Stack:** Rust 1.96, `libghostty-vt = "0.2.2"` (needs Zig 0.15.2 on PATH: `/data/scratch/zig/y/zig-x86_64-linux-0.15.2`; `GHOSTTY_SOURCE_DIR=/data/scratch/s1-probe/target/debug/build/libghostty-vt-sys-90a98b82a8a190aa/out/ghostty-src` avoids the network clone; the PC Docker image already has Zig 0.15.2), `serde`/`serde_json`, `clap`, `anyhow`, `rand` (seeded splits). Python 3 + `pyte 0.8.2` from `~/Others/tmls/.venv` for the portability probe (read-only use of that venv).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Spec:** `docs/PLAN.md` §3 (Emulator core — provisional, gate S1), §5.2 (attach = snapshot at offset S + output from S; portable VT reconstruction with documented limits), §6 row S1 ("libghostty-vt pinned build on Linux + Windows MSVC; recorded Claude sessions; snapshot/restore at adversarial byte boundaries = uninterrupted run; portable VT reconstruction quality. Pass: identical results; differences explained"), §10 risks. Probe facts: `/data/scratch/s1-probe/REPORT.md`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Global Constraints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Linux only tonight; Windows MSVC build is out of scope (laptop needed) — state it in the results.[m
[32m+[m[32m- All scratch/corpus/results under `/data/scratch/s1/` (never `/tmp`; `TMPDIR=/data/scratch/s1`). Recorded corpus files are committed under `spikes/s1/corpus/` only if < 200 KB each; bigger ones stay in `/data/scratch/s1/corpus/` and are referenced by path + sha256.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Never record the user's existing tmux sessions or Claude sessions; the Claude Code recording is a fresh `claude` run under `script` with one trivial prompt and `/exit`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Zig 0.15.2 only (0.16 fails — probe). Pin `libghostty-vt = "=0.2.2"`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `cargo test -p s0` must keep passing without Zig? — No: adding `spikes/s1` to the workspace makes a root `cargo test` need Zig. Ruling: accept; document in `tooling/docker/README.md` and `spikes/s1/README.md` that `-p s0` alone still builds without Zig, and the PC image has Zig.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Commits: author `sgkayast <sgn.kayastha@gmail.com>`, no Claude attribution lines.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Terminology in results: "VT-reconstruction snapshot" (not "native snapshot"); mismatch counts are per cell / per state field; "identical" means `Grid == Grid && TermState == TermState`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Review Focus[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Split inside a multi-byte UTF-8 char or an escape sequence** — expected: the naive strategy shows a mismatch (parser state lost), the sequence-aligned strategy ("tail carry": snapshot at the last complete boundary ≤ p and replay bytes from that boundary) is identical. Test: Task 4 `split_inside_csi_naive_differs_aligned_identical`.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Alternate screen active at the split** — expected: restore lands on the alt screen with the primary screen content preserved; if the Formatter cannot encode both screens, the results doc says so (Task 4 test `alt_screen_split_roundtrip`).[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Scrollback at the split** — expected: `scrollback_rows` and scrollback text equal after restore, or the limit is documented (Task 4 `scrollback_preserved_or_documented`).[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Modes and keyboard protocol** — DECCKM, bracketed paste (2004), mouse tracking (1000/1002/1006), kitty keyboard flags, DECTCEM cursor hidden — expected identical after restore (Task 4 `modes_roundtrip`).[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **Snapshot taken while a hyperlink / wide char / combining sequence is in progress** — expected identical with the aligned strategy (Task 2 corpus includes these; Task 4 compares).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Task 1: Crate skeleton, pinned build, Grid/TermState extraction[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Files:**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Modify: `Cargo.toml` (workspace members += `spikes/s1`)[m
[32m+[m[32m- Create: `spikes/s1/Cargo.toml`, `spikes/s1/README.md`, `spikes/s1/src/lib.rs`, `spikes/s1/src/grid.rs`, `spikes/s1/src/main.rs`, `spikes/s1/build-env.sh`[m
[32m+[m[32m- Test: inline in `grid.rs`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Interfaces:**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Produces: `grid::Cell { text: String, fg: Option<(u8,u8,u8)>, bg: Option<(u8,u8,u8)>, bold: bool, italic: bool, underline: bool, inverse: bool, strike: bool, faint: bool, wide: bool }`, `grid::Grid { cols: u16, rows: u16, cells: Vec<Cell> }` (row-major, `cells.len() == cols*rows`), `grid::TermState { cursor_x: u16, cursor_y: u16, cursor_visible: bool, cursor_style: String, alt_screen: bool, modes: Vec<(String,bool)>, title: String, pwd: String, kitty_flags: u32, scrollback_rows: usize, total_rows: usize }`, `grid::capture(term: &mut Terminal) -> anyhow::Result<(Grid, TermState)>` using `render::RenderState::update` → `RowIterator`/`CellIterator` (`graphemes_utf8`, `fg_color`, `bg_color`, `style()` flags) and `Terminal` getters (`cursor_x/y`, `is_cursor_visible`, `cursor_style`, `active_screen`, `mode(Mode::…)` for the fixed list below, `title`, `pwd`, `kitty_keyboard_flags`, `scrollback_rows`, `total_rows`). `grid::diff(a: &(Grid,TermState), b: &(Grid,TermState)) -> Diff { cell_mismatches: Vec<(u16,u16,Cell,Cell)>, state_mismatches: Vec<(String,String,String)> }`, `Diff::is_identical()`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Mode list (fixed, by name): `cursor_keys (DECCKM 1)`, `origin (6)`, `autowrap (7)`, `cursor_visible (25)`, `alt_screen (1049)`, `bracketed_paste (2004)`, `mouse_normal (1000)`, `mouse_button (1002)`, `mouse_any (1003)`, `mouse_sgr (1006)`, `focus_events (1004)`, `synchronized_output (2026)`, `grapheme_cluster (2027)`. Use the crate's `Mode` enum variants that exist; skip (and list in README) any that are missing.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `build-env.sh`: `export PATH=/data/scratch/zig/y/zig-x86_64-linux-0.15.2:$PATH GHOSTTY_SOURCE_DIR=<probe checkout> TMPDIR=/data/scratch/s1` — sourced before cargo.[m
