 It prints the receiver command to paste into kitty[m
 (`s0 recv --plain --log ~/s0-logs/runs/K1-<id>.recv.jsonl --quit-after N --ack false`; no acks, so the[m
[31m-typed text is not echoed back as noise), waits for the log file, counts down 3 s, then pipes[m
[32m+[m[32mtyped text is not echoed back as noise), waits for the log file, prints "recv is live" and waits 5 s (click the kitty window now), then types a[m
[32m+[m[32m**focus probe** (`x#999999`, seq 999999, out of range: logged by recv but not counted toward `--quit-after`;[m
[32m+[m[32mthe report shows it as `out_of_range 1`, which is expected). The script polls the recv log up to 3 s for[m
[32m+[m[32m`"seq":999999`; if it never appears it prints a red message and **exits 2 without typing the stream**[m
[32m+[m[32m(kitty not focused, or recv not running). On "focus OK" it counts down 3 s, then pipes[m
 `s0 keys --plain --events N` into `ydotool type --key-delay D --file -`, waits for the done line and[m
 prints the `K1-kitty-ydotool` row. Needs `ydotoold`: `systemctl --user start ydotool` (user unit; there is no[m
 system unit on pcl) or `ydotoold --socket-path=/run/user/1000/.ydotool_socket --socket-perm=0600 &` +[m
[1mdiff --git a/spikes/s0/run/k1-keys.sh b/spikes/s0/run/k1-keys.sh[m
